From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:41:48 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: complete exercised WebGL capability queries

Extend the existing query-only Apple A18 Pro / macOS ANGLE profile. Both
HTML and Offscreen contexts now return standard constants and valid scalar
or fresh Float32Array results for the capability queries observed in the
Sephora protection scripts. Include signed texel offsets, uniform/block
limits, varying limits and transform-feedback components. Keep WebGL2-only
queries invalid in WebGL1 and preserve sticky, clear-on-read errors.

Use source-derived ANGLE Metal macOS limits at revision
 a35430f259e8e277253c99cfcb5a0bf9226cdfe5:
- DisplayMtl.mm: macOS varying/output limits, point/line ranges, uniform
  formulas, Apple-family UBO alignment and texel-offset/LOD values.
- mtl_common.h: 16 KiB default uniforms and UBO size, 16 blocks per stage,
  32 combined bindings; combined components = 4096 + 16384*16/4.
- Constants.h: 128 transform-feedback interleaved components.
These are source-backed profile values, not measurements from an A18 Pro
Mac or verification against the exact target Chrome revision.

Expose getContextAttributes with fresh own data properties, requested
creation flags and DOMString/enum conversion. Convert WebGL options before
cache checks as Chrome does, while keeping the cached context's original
attributes. Reject Symbol power preferences and avoid inherited-setter
interference when constructing the returned dictionary. Leave 2D settings
handling outside this patch.

Add the WebGL2-only getInternalformatParameter query for core renderbuffer
formats, with fresh Int32Array results and invalid-enum handling. The human
explicitly approved a conservative synthetic device-dependent policy:
4 maximum/default antialiased samples; non-integer formats report [4,2],
integer formats []; 8-bit color, optional 24-bit depth and 8-bit stencil.
Legacy RGB/RGBA aliases use the corresponding non-integer sample policy.
ANGLE Metal selects its actual sample counts through MTLDevice; these
choices are not claimed as measured hardware support. Framebuffer bit and
sample queries agree with the stored alpha/depth/stencil/antialias flags.

No renderer, shader/resource implementation, SDK rewriting or fingerprint
hash substitution is added. Existing renderer identity, extension list and
shader-precision profile remain unchanged; this is not complete WebGL.

Temporary owned controls: 296/296 API checks pass on patched Debug,
Camoufox158 and Chrome154 across HTML/Offscreen and WebGL1/2; saved0097
passes100/296. Patched native also passes54/54 policy-specific assertions.
Reference device-dependent values are not compared to the mock policy;
reference cached-option conversion, integer samples and RGB/RGBA alias
behavior differ and are recorded separately. Existing Canvas2D108/108 and
upstream1658/1658 tests pass; no upstream tests were added or modified.
Live acceptance is evaluated separately and is not established by these
owned checks.

